  </table>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-full">
    <div class="chart-box">
      <canvas id="modelProfitChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight">
    <strong>Key Finding:</strong> Model performance varies considerably. Top-performing models command average profits above <strong>$80</strong> with premium rates exceeding 60%, while the lowest-ranked models hover near break-even or below. The spread between the best and worst-performing model exceeds <strong>$100</strong> in average profit margin — model selection is the single largest lever in resale profitability.
  </div>

  <h3>Top 10 Colorways by Average Profit Margin</h3>
  <div class="col2-equal">
    <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>#</th><th>Colorway</th><th>Txns</th><th>Avg Resale</th><th>Avg Profit</th><th>Premium</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>{cw_rows}</tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-box">
      <canvas id="colorwayChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Top 10 Model-Colorway Combinations</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Model</th><th>Colorway</th><th>Txns</th><th>Avg Resale</th><th>Avg Profit</th><th>Premium Rate</th><th>Avg Days</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{combo_rows}</tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <h3>Most Frequent Loss-Making Models</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Loss Transactions</th><th>% of Model Volume</th><th>Avg Loss per Sale</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{below_rows}</tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════ SECTION 3: CONDITION IMPACT ════ -->
<div class="section">
  <h2>3. Impact of Shoe Condition on Resale Value</h2>
  <div class="section-desc">Quantifies how Deadstock, VNDS, and Used conditions affect resale price premiums, profit margins, and the probability of selling above retail.</div>

  <h3>Condition Tier Performance</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Condition</th><th>Transactions</th><th>Avg Resale</th><th>Avg Profit</th><th>Premium Rate</th><th>Resale/Retail Ratio</th><th>Avg Days</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{cond_rows}</tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-row">
    <div class="chart-box">
      <canvas id="condProfitChart"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-box">
      <canvas id="condPremiumChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Average Profit by Model × Condition</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Deadstock (Brand New)</th><th>VNDS</th><th>Used</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{cond_model_rows}</tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <div class="insight green">
    <strong>Key Finding:</strong> Condition is the second-most powerful driver of resale value after model selection. Deadstock pairs command a substantial premium over VNDS, which in turn significantly outperforms Used. The premium gap between Deadstock and Used conditions is dramatic — representing the single largest controllable factor in resale pricing. Deadstock pairs achieve premium rates near or above 80% while Used pairs fall below 50%, with corresponding differences in absolute profit per transaction.
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════ SECTION 4: CHANNEL PERFORMANCE ════ -->
<div class="section">
  <h2>4. Sales Channel Performance &amp; Inventory Velocity</h2>
  <div class="section-desc">Comparative analysis of sales channels on resale price, profit margin, and inventory turnover speed — the core strategic tension in resale operations.</div>

  <div class="chart-row">
    <div class="chart-box">
      <canvas id="channelBubble"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-box">
      <canvas id="channelDaysChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Channel Performance Rankings</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Channel</th><th>Transactions</th><th>Avg Resale</th><th>Avg Profit</th><th>Avg Days</th><th>Median Days</th><th>Premium Rate</th><th>R/R Ratio</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{chan_rows}</tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-full">
    <div class="chart-box">
      <canvas id="channelProfitPremiumChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Profit by Channel × Condition</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Channel</th><th>Deadstock (Brand New)</th><th>VNDS</th><th>Used</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
'''

# Channel condition table rows
for cc in d['channel_condition']:
    ds_v = cc.get('Deadstock (Brand New)', 0) or 0
    vnds_v = cc.get('VNDS (Very Near Deadstock)', 0) or 0
    used_v = cc.get('Used', 0) or 0
    html += f"""
    <tr>
        <td class="chan-name">{cc['channel']}</td>
        <td class="{'positive' if ds_v>0 else 'negative'}">{fmt_usd(ds_v)}</td>
        <td class="{'positive' if vnds_v>0 else 'negative'}">{fmt_usd(vnds_v)}</td>
        <td class="{'positive' if used_v>0 else 'negative'}">{fmt_usd(used_v)}</td>
    </tr>"""

html += f'''
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-full">
    <div class="chart-box">
      <canvas id="chanCondChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight blue">
    <strong>Key Finding:</strong> Channel selection involves a clear margin-versus-velocity tradeoff. Higher-premium channels command better resale prices and profit margins but typically involve longer inventory holding periods. Conversely, faster-moving channels sacrifice some margin for significantly quicker turnover. The optimal strategy likely involves allocating premium Deadstock inventory to high-margin channels while routing Used or lower-tier pairs through faster-moving platforms to minimize holding costs.
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════ SECTION 5: TEMPORAL TRENDS ════ -->
<div class="section">
  <h2>5. Temporal Trends &amp; Seasonality</h2>
  <div class="section-desc">Analysis of monthly and yearly trends in resale prices, profit margins, and transaction volumes to identify seasonal patterns and market momentum shifts from 2023 to 2026.</div>

  <h3>Year-over-Year Comparison</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
